// LOCKED RULES - paste into Firebase Console -> Firestore Database -> Rules   for DB-2 (history project) and DB-3 (chat project) ONLY.
//   DB-1 (main project) must use  firestore.rules.DB1-admin-only  - the admin panel pages read/write DB-1 from the browser and a full lock would break them.
//
// After the app uses the load balancer API, the phones must NOT touch Firestore any more.
// Our servers use the Firebase ADMIN SDK, which ignores these rules - so they keep working.
// Firebase Authentication (login / signup / Google) is a different product and is not affected.
//
// Publish this ONLY AFTER the new app version is live (older cached app versions that still talk to Firestore stop working).
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
